WEBVTT


00:00:09.573 --> 00:00:10.798
It's going to come
up in conversations...


00:00:10.894 --> 00:00:12.057
where people say "You
remember when... "


00:00:12.153 --> 00:00:14.628
the closing of California's
IndyMac Bank has resulted in


00:00:14.724 --> 00:00:18.042
what could turn out to be the most
costly bank failure in U.S. history.


00:00:18.138 --> 00:00:20.044
DOW has dropped more
than 800 points...


00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.994
and it's not clear
the crisis is over.


00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.700
Last night there was an
emergency meeting in Washington.


00:00:24.796 --> 00:00:28.572
The leaders of Congress were
told the Nation's financial system


00:00:28.668 --> 00:00:30.780
was facing imminent collapse.


00:00:30.876 --> 00:00:34.707
53,000 City Group workers
are losing their jobs.


00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:55.808
Good morning.


00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.678
Hey.


00:02:04.288 --> 00:02:06.570
Hey, do I have any messages?


00:02:08.277 --> 00:02:12.172
Wilcox want to see you. She's in
the fifth floor conference room.


00:02:12.268 --> 00:02:14.971
Shot an eighty-six at
the club this morning.


00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.187
She said it was important.


00:02:17.255 --> 00:02:20.520
Sally Wilcox thinks
everything's important.


00:02:20.616 --> 00:02:22.534
Thank you.


00:02:29.052 --> 00:02:30.467
Anyone want to
take a guess at what


00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:31.853
I shot at the club this morning?


00:02:31.949 --> 00:02:34.313
Go ahead, take a shot. Just...


00:02:35.172 --> 00:02:36.342
No?


00:02:36.437 --> 00:02:38.183
44 on the front, 42 on the back.


00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:42.001
Oh, no you didn't,
Bob! Yes, I really did.


00:02:42.422 --> 00:02:43.900
It's true.


00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:46.278
What happened, somebody die?


00:02:50.058 --> 00:02:51.534
Conal?


00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.067
They closed Mobile
and Newport News.


00:02:54.162 --> 00:02:56.637
They merged Ship Systems
into Rail Products.


00:02:56.733 --> 00:02:58.057
How many?


00:02:58.153 --> 00:03:00.354
Conal, your wife is on one.


00:03:03.505 --> 00:03:05.961
Hi, honey.
- Three thousand at the shipyards.


00:03:06.056 --> 00:03:08.262
Rumor is, another
couple hundred here.


00:03:08.358 --> 00:03:10.559
Uh, I've got some bad news.


00:03:18.218 --> 00:03:19.398
What's going on?


00:03:19.494 --> 00:03:22.073
Bobby, you know Dick
Landry from Legal.


00:03:22.169 --> 00:03:24.145
The company's
consolidating divisions.


00:03:24.241 --> 00:03:25.614
Difficult decisions
had to be made in...


00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.870
areas where
redundancies surfaced.


00:03:26.965 --> 00:03:29.171
We've stuctured a generous
severance package for you.


00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.672
Your twelve years with
us entitles you to...


00:03:32.768 --> 00:03:35.702
twelve weeks full
pay, and benefits.


00:03:36.442 --> 00:03:38.724
You're firing me?
- Come on, Bobby, sit down.


00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.950
We're also offering you
outplacement services...


00:03:41.046 --> 00:03:43.059
to help you secure
your next employment.


00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:46.416
Does Gene know about this?
- Please, sit.


00:03:51.595 --> 00:03:53.514
You know what, Sally?


00:03:53.936 --> 00:03:55.855
Fuck off!


00:03:59.231 --> 00:04:02.492
Is Gene in here?
- He's in Chicago today.


00:04:03.566 --> 00:04:06.417
We've reviewed our pipeline
of some 500 projects...


00:04:06.513 --> 00:04:08.227
and programs. Focusing on those


00:04:08.323 --> 00:04:09.380
with significant marketing...


00:04:09.476 --> 00:04:10.837
opportunities,
jettisoning everything


00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:13.666
that won't contribute
immediately to our profitability.


00:04:13.762 --> 00:04:15.872
Selecting thirty-seven
as promising...


00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.397
strategic growth programs,


00:04:17.492 --> 00:04:19.891
and setting aside the rest
for future consideration.


00:04:19.987 --> 00:04:21.943
Ned Haspel, JP Morgan.


00:04:22.058 --> 00:04:25.875
Mr. McClary, you were talking
earlier about Fiscal 2011.


00:04:25.971 --> 00:04:28.744
You've done a good job of
convincing us that with the...


00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.210
credit markets frozen
your sales revenue in 2010


00:04:31.305 --> 00:04:34.854
will slow- - Great,
then my job here is done!


00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.194
Can you talk about
2011 and what sort...


00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.534
of a percentage
increase you anticipate?


00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.526
We all like to talk
percentages, Ned.


00:04:41.622 --> 00:04:43.150
Your people do, our people do.


00:04:43.246 --> 00:04:45.452
Are you suggesting that
you aren't expecting...


00:04:45.548 --> 00:04:47.322
any growth in your
division next year?


00:04:47.418 --> 00:04:50.862
I'm suggesting that we face
increased foreign competition,


00:04:50.958 --> 00:04:53.384
and a difficult credit market
for large capital expenditures -


00:04:53.479 --> 00:04:54.296
like ship building.


00:04:54.392 --> 00:04:57.585
So... no growth in 2011?


00:04:59.043 --> 00:05:03.887
I am confident that while ship
building will remain challenged,


00:05:03.983 --> 00:05:05.578
the rest of the
Transportation Systems


00:05:05.674 --> 00:05:07.312
Group will continue
to make significant


00:05:07.408 --> 00:05:11.728
contributions to growth at
GTX in the coming quarters.


00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:14.428
Yes, in the back.


00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.312
Honesty's the best policy?


00:05:22.408 --> 00:05:25.075
Christ, could you just try to
be a little less candid for once?


00:05:25.171 --> 00:05:27.159
So we're lying to
financial analysts now?


00:05:27.255 --> 00:05:28.796
That the new profitability plan?


00:05:28.892 --> 00:05:31.244
What do you want? More
inflated guidance so we...


00:05:31.339 --> 00:05:33.937
can underperform in all four
quarters again next year?


00:05:34.032 --> 00:05:38.027
2011? I'm worried about
our share price tomorrow.


00:05:38.829 --> 00:05:42.334
Salinger is going to
blow a fucking gasket.


00:05:54.174 --> 00:05:56.092
Oh shit...


00:05:57.858 --> 00:05:59.776
Yeah.
- They...


00:06:00.122 --> 00:06:02.731
...say who else is on the block?


00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.905
Thanks for the sympathy, Phil.


00:06:10.826 --> 00:06:13.109
Call you later, okay?
- Okay.


00:06:16.772 --> 00:06:19.870
Did they say anything about me?
- What?


00:06:20.532 --> 00:06:22.701
About my still having a job?


00:06:22.797 --> 00:06:24.829
You know, I didn't ask.


00:07:17.276 --> 00:07:19.443
I've been trying to reach you.
- This damn thing's dead.


00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:23.088
Recharge it for me, will you?
- Phil's in there.


00:07:23.184 --> 00:07:25.045
Make yourself
right at home, Phil.


00:07:25.141 --> 00:07:27.922
I won't go back to
the factory floor!


00:07:28.018 --> 00:07:30.937
I've got one kid in college,
another one going in the Fall.


00:07:31.032 --> 00:07:32.794
What the hell are
you talking about?


00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.416
You're shitting
me! He doesn't know?


00:07:34.512 --> 00:07:36.670
Sally Wilcox let
some more people go.


00:07:36.766 --> 00:07:39.010
Some! She fired
goddam everybody!


00:07:39.106 --> 00:07:40.065
Did she fire you?


00:07:40.161 --> 00:07:42.271
No, but I've been
hiding in here all day!


00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.342
They closed Mobile
and Newport News.


00:07:44.438 --> 00:07:46.491
Laid off most of the
Ship Systems Sales Group.


00:07:46.587 --> 00:07:49.368
I won't let the bastards just
kick me out after 30 years.


00:07:49.464 --> 00:07:53.377
I'll take an AK-47 to
this fuckin' place, first!


00:08:01.397 --> 00:08:02.547
What were you going
to do? Let me...


00:08:02.643 --> 00:08:03.793
read about it in
tomorrow's Journal?


00:08:03.889 --> 00:08:05.601
We're in the middle
of something here-


00:08:05.697 --> 00:08:07.093
You closed two of my ship yards?


00:08:07.189 --> 00:08:10.047
Consolidating divisions has
been under discussion for months.


00:08:10.143 --> 00:08:11.659
Yeah, and I told you
it was a shitty idea.


00:08:11.755 --> 00:08:13.566
We took that opinion
into consideration.


00:08:13.662 --> 00:08:14.728
It's my goddam division!


00:08:14.824 --> 00:08:16.742
It's my goddam company!


00:08:21.385 --> 00:08:24.727
Would you excuse us
for a moment, please.


00:08:30.363 --> 00:08:32.760
Don't embarrass me like that...
- (scoffs) Embarrass you?


00:08:32.856 --> 00:08:35.177
I'm gone one day and you
gut one of my divisions?


00:08:35.273 --> 00:08:37.555
Stock's stalled,
revenues are flat.


00:08:37.651 --> 00:08:39.714
The entire economy is flat
- we're in the middle of a recession.


00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.130
I only closed two
of the ship yards,


00:08:41.226 --> 00:08:42.658
I should have closed
all three of them.


00:08:42.754 --> 00:08:45.920
Our stock is in the fucking toilet!
- Everybody's stock is in the toilet.


00:08:46.016 --> 00:08:47.917
Well, the stockholders
would like to...


00:08:48.013 --> 00:08:49.564
see their share value maximized.


00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.024
Well, sell the fucking Degas.


00:08:58.101 --> 00:09:00.307
Well, now, I heard you put
on quite a show in Chicago.


00:09:00.403 --> 00:09:02.382
What'd you do? You told
a room full of analysts...


00:09:02.478 --> 00:09:04.336
we weren't gonna generate
any growth next year?


00:09:04.431 --> 00:09:05.639
Three thousand jobs?


00:09:05.735 --> 00:09:07.990
Gene, we're not some shitty
little shipyard any more!


00:09:08.086 --> 00:09:10.436
I'm not going to keep pouring
money into a losing operation.


00:09:10.532 --> 00:09:11.751
We innovate,
we re-tool-


00:09:11.847 --> 00:09:15.189
Ah, American heavy
manufacturing is dead.


00:09:15.557 --> 00:09:18.981
Steel, autos, your
precious ship building.


00:09:19.969 --> 00:09:21.452
The future is in heathcare...


00:09:21.548 --> 00:09:23.402
infrastructure and
power generation.


00:09:23.498 --> 00:09:25.584
I have to be involved
in any decision...


00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:27.393
that affects one
of my divisions.


00:09:27.489 --> 00:09:30.423
You wouldn't have
approved the cuts.


00:09:30.865 --> 00:09:34.414
You'd have gone behind my back
to the Board again! Right...?


00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.711
They were good people, Jim.


00:09:39.114 --> 00:09:41.243
They're not our responsibility.


00:09:41.339 --> 00:09:44.029
We work for the
stockholders now!


00:09:54.077 --> 00:09:55.554
Your dad's home?


00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.050
Yeah.


00:09:57.146 --> 00:10:01.059
Can you grab the rest of
these out of the trunk?


00:10:04.244 --> 00:10:05.951
Hey!


00:10:06.047 --> 00:10:09.226
What're you doing home?
- Making dinner.


00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:12.857
We're going over to Jack's.
- That's tonight?


00:10:13.068 --> 00:10:14.986
Dierdre's birthday.


00:10:16.329 --> 00:10:17.515
I think it's gonna rain.


00:10:17.611 --> 00:10:19.724
You know what? You
don't wanna come, fine.


00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.298
Don't come!


00:10:21.393 --> 00:10:23.312
Thanks, bud.


00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.532
Drew, can you finish
that upstairs, please?


00:10:35.628 --> 00:10:38.296
Can you put on clean
pair of jeans, please.


00:10:38.391 --> 00:10:41.439
We're going over to your
Uncle Jack's for dinner.


00:10:41.535 --> 00:10:42.560
Christ, you don't
have to like him,


00:10:42.656 --> 00:10:43.988
but you could pretend,
for my sake. I mean...


00:10:44.084 --> 00:10:45.618
he doesn't like you either,
but at least he cares...


00:10:45.714 --> 00:10:47.309
enough about me to not treat
you like a piece of shit.


00:10:47.405 --> 00:10:49.323
They fired me.


00:10:51.626 --> 00:10:54.848
What?
- They... fired me.


00:10:55.577 --> 00:10:57.495
Today.


00:10:57.956 --> 00:11:00.334
Sally Wilcox.
- Why?


00:11:02.252 --> 00:11:04.616
Something about redundancies.


00:11:06.109 --> 00:11:09.791
Gene said you were safe!
- Gene said a lot of things...


00:11:09.887 --> 00:11:11.797
but he was nowhere
to be found today.


00:11:11.893 --> 00:11:13.261
Bobby, you busted
your ass for them!


00:11:13.357 --> 00:11:15.355
No, no, I'm sorry fuck them
and fuck Gene McClary...


00:11:15.451 --> 00:11:17.370
and all his promises!


00:11:19.173 --> 00:11:21.091
Something's burning.


00:11:36.053 --> 00:11:37.971
Hey, I, uh...


00:11:38.125 --> 00:11:40.888
I don't wanna tell
anybody, you know...


00:11:40.984 --> 00:11:42.594
'til I get another job.


00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.608
Alright?


00:12:19.177 --> 00:12:21.095
Hey.


00:12:21.746 --> 00:12:23.664
Where's your mom?


00:12:23.934 --> 00:12:25.852
Headache.


00:12:28.614 --> 00:12:33.587
Oh, Dad! They announced where
we're going for our senior trip.


00:12:34.062 --> 00:12:36.594
Italy.
- Italy?


00:12:38.359 --> 00:12:41.122
Wow! Boy, that's great.


00:12:41.926 --> 00:12:43.844
I can go, right?


00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.825
Yeah... Of course, sweetheart.


00:13:13.962 --> 00:13:15.880
Phil?
- Yeah.


00:13:17.339 --> 00:13:19.257
Oh, God.


00:13:21.981 --> 00:13:26.508
Ann Doherty called.
- They fired Conal.


00:13:29.309 --> 00:13:31.381
Are we okay?
- Yeah.


00:13:36.138 --> 00:13:38.305
I should get ready.
- For what?


00:13:38.401 --> 00:13:40.684
We've got Salinger's dinner.


00:13:40.703 --> 00:13:41.723
Oh God, I completely forgot.


00:13:41.819 --> 00:13:43.830
You don't have to come if
you're not feeling up to it.


00:13:43.926 --> 00:13:47.024
Just gimme a minute
to put my face on.


00:14:08.404 --> 00:14:10.557
Gene...? Where've you been?


00:14:10.653 --> 00:14:13.914
The car's picking us
up in half-an-hour.


00:14:15.425 --> 00:14:18.393
I really don't want
to be late again.


00:14:18.489 --> 00:14:21.668
Can we please try
not to be late again?


00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:27.558
Stephanie finally found a
table. For the window? I like it.


00:14:36.123 --> 00:14:38.386
George Hepplewhite
fruitwood table...


00:14:38.482 --> 00:14:43.781
...With paint and inlay decorations.
Circa 1820, Price: $ 16750.00


00:15:08.753 --> 00:15:10.672
I'm coming.


00:15:11.554 --> 00:15:13.472
Hi.


00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:18.479
Hi, how are you? How you doing?
- Good, good, thanks.


00:15:29.547 --> 00:15:32.789
How go the suit wars, Bobby?
- Alright, Jack.


00:15:32.885 --> 00:15:35.506
Move any more high
paying American jobs...


00:15:35.602 --> 00:15:37.969
offshore to Asian
shitholes this week?


00:15:38.065 --> 00:15:39.762
Mostly focused on
union busting now.


00:15:39.858 --> 00:15:40.731
You know how it is.


00:15:40.827 --> 00:15:45.473
Surprised you could make it.
No early flight or golf game?


00:15:46.199 --> 00:15:48.327
Those are the usual
excuses, aren't they?


00:15:48.423 --> 00:15:50.975
Aww hey, Bobby.
- Hey! Birthday girl.


00:15:51.071 --> 00:15:52.357
I can't believe
you're thirty-five.


00:15:52.453 --> 00:15:54.121
I mean, you don't look
a day over twenty-one.


00:15:54.217 --> 00:15:56.269
Aww, see Jack, now
that's how it's done.


00:15:56.365 --> 00:15:59.224
You're a liar Bobby,
but I love you for it.


00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:01.128
You need to get back to
your post, barbecue boy.


00:16:01.224 --> 00:16:01.833
Alright, alright.


00:16:01.928 --> 00:16:03.500
Why don't you grab
yourself a drink, Bobby.


00:16:03.596 --> 00:16:05.056
We got some margaritas
in the blender...


00:16:05.152 --> 00:16:06.705
and we got some beers
out back in the cooler.


00:16:06.801 --> 00:16:08.719
Thanks.


00:16:20.689 --> 00:16:22.607
Now there's action!


00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:27.447
Who better to present this
year's Man of the Year Award...


00:16:27.595 --> 00:16:30.099
than the man who's known
him longer than anyone else.


00:16:30.195 --> 00:16:32.218
Gene McClary is Executive
Vice-President...


00:16:32.314 --> 00:16:35.076
of GTX Global
Transportation Systems.


00:16:35.172 --> 00:16:37.858
He's also, I'm
told, one of GTX's...


00:16:37.954 --> 00:16:40.984
first employees. Gene McClary.


00:16:48.312 --> 00:16:50.230
Thank you.


00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.680
Actually, if memory serves,


00:16:52.776 --> 00:16:54.892
I was GTX's only
employee at the time.


00:16:54.988 --> 00:16:57.128
Nobody wanted
Gloucester Shipbuilding,


00:16:57.224 --> 00:16:59.305
years of multi-million
dollar losses,


00:16:59.401 --> 00:17:01.718
the highest labor
costs in the industry.


00:17:01.814 --> 00:17:03.716
But from those
humble beginnings,


00:17:03.812 --> 00:17:06.699
Jim was able to grow
Gloucester into GTX...


00:17:06.795 --> 00:17:09.432
with sixty thousand employees
and eleven billion dollars


00:17:09.528 --> 00:17:11.485
in gross annual revenue.


00:17:17.203 --> 00:17:22.803
So it is my priviledge to
introduce my oldest friend,


00:17:24.491 --> 00:17:26.409
college roommate,


00:17:26.525 --> 00:17:28.534
the best Man at my
wedding and the...


00:17:28.629 --> 00:17:30.304
worst tennis player I ever met.


00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.905
Ladies and Gentlemen.
My boss, Jim Salinger.


00:17:39.608 --> 00:17:41.864
Thank you, ladies and
gentlemen. Without a doubt...


00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.042
you don't build a company


00:17:43.138 --> 00:17:46.685
like GTX without the
support and leadership...


00:17:46.781 --> 00:17:48.982
of a man like Gene McClary.


00:17:57.026 --> 00:17:58.944
Executive offices.


00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:01.898
Hi, Bobby Walker, GTX.


00:18:01.937 --> 00:18:03.855
Down on your left.


00:18:18.895 --> 00:18:20.813
Nice suit.


00:18:21.427 --> 00:18:23.345
Thanks.
- Orientation?


00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:26.836
Yeah.
- That way.


00:18:27.258 --> 00:18:28.850
Oh, thanks.
- Do "The Tiger" for me.


00:18:28.946 --> 00:18:30.864
What?
- Down the hall.


00:18:31.018 --> 00:18:32.496
Thanks.


00:18:32.592 --> 00:18:35.756
First, let me tell you
what outplacement is not.


00:18:35.851 --> 00:18:37.483
We're not an employment agency.


00:18:37.579 --> 00:18:40.595
We're here to help
you help yourself.


00:18:40.763 --> 00:18:42.214
Now you all need
to put together...


00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:43.889
a networking list
of all your friends.


00:18:43.985 --> 00:18:46.230
That's suppliers, competitors,


00:18:46.326 --> 00:18:48.225
people you sat next
to at a convention,


00:18:48.321 --> 00:18:51.410
neighbors, dentists.
Anybody and everybody.


00:18:51.506 --> 00:18:53.991
You need a new
resume. You're going...


00:18:54.087 --> 00:18:56.972
to be sending out
hundreds, so make it good.


00:18:57.068 --> 00:18:58.815
Endings.


00:18:58.911 --> 00:19:03.361
We're not used to them.
Fear, anxiety, loss.


00:19:03.629 --> 00:19:06.971
How many of you are
feeling these things?


00:19:08.886 --> 00:19:13.949
Endings, fear,
change, and finally...


00:19:15.062 --> 00:19:16.347
Success.


00:19:16.443 --> 00:19:18.926
Okay, everybody up. C'mon,
no use sitting around...


00:19:19.022 --> 00:19:20.759
feeling sorry for
ourselves. Up, UP.


00:19:20.855 --> 00:19:23.835
This is called "The Tiger", we do
it when we need get our energy up.


00:19:23.931 --> 00:19:26.801
I... Will... Win.


00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:30.111
Why? I'll show you why!


00:19:30.207 --> 00:19:33.555
Because I have
- Faith! Courage! Enthusiasm!


00:19:33.651 --> 00:19:35.147
Everybody this time.


00:19:35.243 --> 00:19:39.079
No thanks.
- I... Will... Win.


00:19:39.885 --> 00:19:40.844
Why?


00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:44.268
Because I have
- Faith! Courage! Enthusiasm!


00:19:44.364 --> 00:19:46.522
Good. I... Will... Win.


00:19:47.136 --> 00:19:48.536
Did Bobby Walker call back?


00:19:48.632 --> 00:19:50.493
Yeah, last night.
- He leave a message?


00:19:50.588 --> 00:19:51.617
Not one I'd care to repeat.


00:19:51.712 --> 00:19:53.179
See if he can come
by for lunch today.


00:19:53.275 --> 00:19:55.538
Stock's up six. Not bad.


00:19:55.807 --> 00:19:57.725
My 401K is all GTX.


00:19:58.032 --> 00:20:01.351
This continues, I may get
to retire before I'm eighty.


00:20:01.447 --> 00:20:03.137
With Ship Systems
and Rail Products...


00:20:03.232 --> 00:20:04.420
merging, we are reassigning


00:20:04.516 --> 00:20:06.434
sales regions.


00:20:06.435 --> 00:20:08.409
How are we doing
with Royal Caribbean?


00:20:08.505 --> 00:20:10.493
They're nervous,
don't like seeing us...


00:20:10.589 --> 00:20:12.323
on Bloomberg every
fifteen minutes.


00:20:12.419 --> 00:20:14.280
Well calm 'em down,
we need that boat.


00:20:14.376 --> 00:20:15.743
How're we supposed
to cover the same...


00:20:15.839 --> 00:20:17.206
number of accounts
with half the staff?


00:20:17.302 --> 00:20:18.433
I'm already gone two
weeks out of four,


00:20:18.529 --> 00:20:20.293
what am I supposed
to tell my kids?


00:20:20.389 --> 00:20:22.567
Tell 'em you're lucky
you still have a job.


00:20:22.663 --> 00:20:24.112
Inactive accounts.


00:20:24.208 --> 00:20:27.538
I want to know what
we're going to do to...


00:20:27.634 --> 00:20:30.895
get the business
back. Client by client.


00:20:34.633 --> 00:20:36.551
It's taken.


00:20:37.012 --> 00:20:38.143
Alright.


00:20:38.239 --> 00:20:40.157
Hey.


00:20:40.734 --> 00:20:42.804
Come in here.
- Thanks.


00:20:44.646 --> 00:20:46.564
Appreciate it.


00:20:47.831 --> 00:20:49.615
Friendly bunch.
- You are the enemy.


00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:51.993
Another warm body they
gotta claw their way over


00:20:52.089 --> 00:20:53.604
to get back to the
corporate food trough.


00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:54.870
And yet, you're not threatened.


00:20:54.966 --> 00:20:56.885
I'm a very secure individual.


00:20:56.981 --> 00:20:59.781
Besides, you do not
look like an engineer.


00:20:59.877 --> 00:21:01.795
MBA?
- Yeah.


00:21:02.256 --> 00:21:04.063
If you knew your way around
a guided missile system,


00:21:04.159 --> 00:21:06.074
I'd have shove an ice pick
into the base of your skull.


00:21:06.169 --> 00:21:07.129
Damn right.


00:21:07.224 --> 00:21:09.450
Your previous employer
has spared no expense.


00:21:09.546 --> 00:21:11.747
Fax machine, Xerox, coffee.


00:21:12.999 --> 00:21:13.845
How was your orientation?


00:21:13.941 --> 00:21:15.646
I felt like someone was
going to shave my head...


00:21:15.742 --> 00:21:17.698
and make me beat a drum.


00:21:18.025 --> 00:21:19.581
What... uh, what do
you gotta do to...


00:21:19.677 --> 00:21:21.189
get yourself in one
of those offices?


00:21:21.285 --> 00:21:23.492
Your company has to pay
extra for one of those.


00:21:23.588 --> 00:21:25.486
Exec V.P.'s and above, mostly.


00:21:25.582 --> 00:21:29.414
That corner one has an
Eastman-Kodak CFO in it.


00:21:29.611 --> 00:21:31.088
How long they give you?


00:21:31.184 --> 00:21:32.467
Three months full
salary, four...


00:21:32.563 --> 00:21:33.927
months outplacement.
How about you?


00:21:34.023 --> 00:21:36.402
Nine months of both.


00:21:37.207 --> 00:21:38.449
I've been here four.


00:21:38.545 --> 00:21:40.948
It won't take me
more than a few days.


00:21:41.044 --> 00:21:42.962
No offense.


00:21:44.382 --> 00:21:46.301
None taken.


00:21:50.942 --> 00:21:52.860
Sorry I'm late,


00:21:53.629 --> 00:21:55.748
how you holding up?
- Good.


00:21:55.930 --> 00:21:57.330
Maggie all right?


00:21:57.426 --> 00:21:59.872
Yeah, she's great, we're fine.


00:22:00.304 --> 00:22:02.222
Glenlivet, rocks.


00:22:06.404 --> 00:22:08.442
It wasn't my call, Bobby.


00:22:09.818 --> 00:22:11.871
Salinger's under a lot of pressure
to boost the stock price...


00:22:11.967 --> 00:22:13.922
before someone
buys in and makes...


00:22:14.018 --> 00:22:15.401
him break up the company.


00:22:15.497 --> 00:22:17.101
We'd lose a lot more
jobs in a merger...


00:22:17.197 --> 00:22:18.471
than we have in this downsizing.


00:22:18.566 --> 00:22:21.539
You trying to appeal to my sense
of the greater corporate good?


00:22:21.635 --> 00:22:23.394
I've been calling
in some markers.


00:22:23.490 --> 00:22:26.258
Tom Borden over at Lockheed,
Pat Leahy at Raytheon...


00:22:26.354 --> 00:22:29.125
You oughta recognize
most of them.


00:22:33.725 --> 00:22:36.660
Come on, let's get
something to eat.


00:22:37.365 --> 00:22:40.055
No thanks. I've
lost my appetite.


00:22:40.933 --> 00:22:42.564
Take the names, Bobby.


00:22:42.659 --> 00:22:44.252
Don't bother
reassigning my accounts.


00:22:44.348 --> 00:22:47.480
I'm gonna steal them
back from you when


00:22:47.575 --> 00:22:50.266
I get a job with
the competition.


00:23:03.031 --> 00:23:04.949
Hey.
- Hey.


00:23:12.661 --> 00:23:13.879
Hey.
- Hey.


00:23:13.975 --> 00:23:15.712
How'd it go?
- Great.


00:23:15.808 --> 00:23:16.721
Yup?
- Yeah.


00:23:16.817 --> 00:23:17.401
Alright.


00:23:17.497 --> 00:23:21.165
I had lunch with Gene,
he gave me some names.


00:23:21.486 --> 00:23:23.404
That's big of him.


00:23:23.443 --> 00:23:25.092
Yeah, I mean, he didn't
have to do anything, ya know.


00:23:25.188 --> 00:23:26.147
Yeah.


00:23:26.243 --> 00:23:28.161
What, what is all this?


00:23:28.621 --> 00:23:31.250
Uh, our mortgage is
resetting next month.


00:23:31.346 --> 00:23:34.309
With that, and the... paying
off the orthodontist...


00:23:34.404 --> 00:23:36.324
and last summers
Disneyworld trip,


00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:38.635
we don't have much
of a cushion left.


00:23:38.731 --> 00:23:40.150
We don't need a cushion.


00:23:40.246 --> 00:23:44.141
The Porsche payments, the credit
cards, your Patriots tickets.


00:23:44.237 --> 00:23:46.635
I told you, I'm splitting the
Pats tickets with Darryl this year.


00:23:46.731 --> 00:23:49.143
Okay, well, just eating
out and doing the damn...


00:23:49.239 --> 00:23:51.852
dry cleaning is costing us
six hundred bucks a month.


00:23:51.948 --> 00:23:53.751
I was thinking maybe I
could go back to work.


00:23:53.847 --> 00:23:54.806
Nuh-uh.


00:23:54.902 --> 00:23:57.377
Not full-time, just
a few shifts a week.


00:23:57.473 --> 00:23:59.027
No.


00:23:59.123 --> 00:24:01.169
3M needs a new
General Sales Manager,


00:24:01.265 --> 00:24:02.519
I called Brian Collins,


00:24:02.615 --> 00:24:04.224
I'm gonna have breakfast
with him next week.


00:24:04.320 --> 00:24:05.741
Okay, but we're gonna
need to cut back.


00:24:05.837 --> 00:24:08.551
Cancel skiing at Christmas, stop
paying the club dues for a while...


00:24:08.647 --> 00:24:10.843
If things get really bad,
I can bag groceries...


00:24:10.939 --> 00:24:14.987
I can be on the corner- -
Don't be a jerk. Okay? Just-


00:24:15.083 --> 00:24:18.670
No more big purchases.
Just eat at home more.


00:24:20.455 --> 00:24:22.373
Hello...


00:24:22.411 --> 00:24:24.329
Hey, Kevin. Yeah.


00:24:25.173 --> 00:24:26.554
Yeah, let me get him
for you, he's right here.


00:24:26.650 --> 00:24:27.609
What?


00:24:27.705 --> 00:24:29.757
He read about the
layoffs in the paper.


00:24:29.853 --> 00:24:31.637
So what?
- You gonna tell him?


00:24:31.733 --> 00:24:35.481
No, I'm not goig to tell
him, because I don't...


00:24:35.577 --> 00:24:39.816
need a lecture on paternal
responsibility right now.


00:24:40.673 --> 00:24:42.793
Hey, Dad. What's going on?


00:24:42.821 --> 00:24:46.001
No, that's... that's
all manufacturing.


00:24:46.044 --> 00:24:49.862
They tried to offer me the C.E.O.
job, I had to turn them down-


00:24:49.958 --> 00:24:55.031
I come bearing gifts; Glenfiddich.
40 year old single malt.


00:24:55.127 --> 00:24:57.083
Nice!
- Ah, it better be.


00:24:58.283 --> 00:25:01.218
Strick sent it
over. That bastard...


00:25:05.189 --> 00:25:07.376
That's Alaska.
- Yeah.


00:25:07.721 --> 00:25:10.657
God dammit, Gene,
those were good times.


00:25:10.752 --> 00:25:12.671
The best.


00:25:13.515 --> 00:25:16.947
Well... you and Cynthia
thinking about joining us...


00:25:17.043 --> 00:25:19.940
at Sun Valley for New
Years again this year?


00:25:20.036 --> 00:25:22.342
I don't know if we can,
Liam's been talking about...


00:25:22.437 --> 00:25:24.698
coming home for Christmas
with Susan and the kids-


00:25:24.794 --> 00:25:28.304
Ah hell, bring them along,
Grandpa! Kay would...


00:25:28.400 --> 00:25:31.613
probably think she'd
died and gone to heaven


00:25:31.708 --> 00:25:34.404
with a bunch of
kids running around.


00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:37.551
I can't have you challenging
me in front of senior staff.


00:25:37.647 --> 00:25:40.279
They respect you.
If you question...


00:25:40.375 --> 00:25:43.305
my judgement you
undermine my authority.


00:25:43.401 --> 00:25:47.314
I need to know, can I
count on your full support?


00:25:50.690 --> 00:25:52.608
Good.


00:26:06.075 --> 00:26:07.993
You okay?


00:26:09.989 --> 00:26:11.535
I had lunch with
Bobby Walker today.


00:26:11.631 --> 00:26:13.844
I thought he was going to
throw a drink in my face.


00:26:13.940 --> 00:26:17.119
You were his boss
Gene, not his father.


00:26:20.117 --> 00:26:22.483
Sue and I were thinking
about sneaking down to


00:26:22.579 --> 00:26:24.893
Palm Beach for a weekend
later on this month.


00:26:24.989 --> 00:26:27.794
You know, some
shopping, some golf.


00:26:27.890 --> 00:26:31.721
Think you can get us one
of the corporate jets?


00:26:33.392 --> 00:26:35.770
Fine, we'll fly commercial.


00:26:38.417 --> 00:26:40.643
Stock closed up two today.


00:26:41.142 --> 00:26:44.710
My options are worth
half-a-million dollars...


00:26:44.806 --> 00:26:47.903
more than when I
woke up this morning.


00:27:04.085 --> 00:27:06.531
Need me to stay, Mr. Woodward?


00:27:07.423 --> 00:27:09.456
Ah... No thanks, Nan.


00:27:11.681 --> 00:27:13.599
See you tomorrow.


00:28:10.189 --> 00:28:12.590
Don't even think about
eating all the candy...


00:28:12.686 --> 00:28:14.927
you get at school.
Three pieces, that's it.


00:28:15.023 --> 00:28:17.877
You look disgusting.
You know that?


00:28:21.738 --> 00:28:25.406
So, I called Bridget
and made an appointment.


00:28:25.650 --> 00:28:27.568
Who?
- The realtor.


00:28:29.678 --> 00:28:32.115
I think we should
at least list it.


00:28:32.211 --> 00:28:34.657
See if we get any offers.
- We're not gonna sell the house.


00:28:34.753 --> 00:28:36.074
Well, we don't need
to accept an offer,


00:28:36.170 --> 00:28:37.141
and with the market so bad...


00:28:37.237 --> 00:28:40.479
it might take a while to sell
it. You know... if we get stuck.


00:28:40.575 --> 00:28:42.939
We're not going to get stuck.


00:28:47.519 --> 00:28:50.665
How do I look?
- Highly employable.


00:28:55.115 --> 00:28:57.033
Okay.


00:28:59.872 --> 00:29:01.790
Bridget?


00:29:02.750 --> 00:29:05.848
C'mon, we're not
gonna sell the house.


00:29:06.472 --> 00:29:08.697
Have a good day.
- Okay.


00:29:20.245 --> 00:29:21.809
Alright Brit, give
me a call next week,


00:29:21.905 --> 00:29:23.179
I should have an answer for you.


00:29:23.275 --> 00:29:25.965
Alright, who's next?
- Mr. Walker.


00:29:26.229 --> 00:29:30.240
Mr. Walker, Joyce Robertson.
Sorry to keep you waiting.


00:29:30.336 --> 00:29:32.521
Would you mind if I have
something to eat here?


00:29:32.616 --> 00:29:34.421
I have another meeting
right after you.


00:29:34.517 --> 00:29:35.476
Go right ahead.


00:29:35.572 --> 00:29:37.759
So, it looks like you worked
for GTX for twelve years.


00:29:37.855 --> 00:29:40.214
I did, Divisional Sales Leader
for three of those years.


00:29:40.310 --> 00:29:43.974
Well, I'm surprised they let you go.
- You and me, both.


00:29:44.070 --> 00:29:45.921
Have you handled regional sales?


00:29:46.017 --> 00:29:47.607
I came up in
regional sales. I...


00:29:47.703 --> 00:29:49.691
worked for Martin-Marietta
in California.


00:29:49.787 --> 00:29:52.317
Well, we're looking to
expand in the South;...


00:29:52.413 --> 00:29:54.103
we need someone in Little Rock.


00:29:54.199 --> 00:29:56.117
In Arkansas?


00:29:56.500 --> 00:30:00.030
Is relocation a problem?
- Ah, no, no.


00:30:00.798 --> 00:30:04.260
I had hoped to stay here,
because I'm from the area-


00:30:04.356 --> 00:30:08.489
You left the salary space
blank on your application.


00:30:08.585 --> 00:30:12.422
Well, you know,
that's a negotiation.


00:30:12.883 --> 00:30:15.100
I was making 120 at
GTX, plus incentives,


00:30:15.196 --> 00:30:17.468
but I know that times
are different now...


00:30:17.564 --> 00:30:21.190
and I'd be willing to
accept 110, hope for bonuses.


00:30:21.286 --> 00:30:24.517
Well, our base salary is
sixty-five thousand a year for


00:30:24.613 --> 00:30:26.651
regional sales sirectors.


00:30:28.037 --> 00:30:30.627
I responded to an ad for the
Vice-President of Marketing.


00:30:30.723 --> 00:30:32.327
Well, we've had a
number of highly...


00:30:32.423 --> 00:30:34.118
qualified applicants
for that position.


00:30:34.214 --> 00:30:38.371
I'M a highly qualified
applicant for that position!


00:30:39.393 --> 00:30:43.551
I'm a HIGHLY qualified
applicant for that position!


00:30:45.609 --> 00:30:49.887
Excuse me, I'm sorry. I must
have had too many cups of coffee


00:30:49.983 --> 00:30:52.688
while I was sitting in your
fucking waiting room for two hours.


00:30:52.784 --> 00:30:54.807
Thanks for your time, Joyce.
And just between the two of us...


00:30:54.903 --> 00:30:57.401
you can probably
skip the Diet Cokes.


00:30:57.497 --> 00:30:58.826
They're not helping.


00:30:58.921 --> 00:31:01.358
Jim's worried,
thinks we're a target.


00:31:01.454 --> 00:31:02.836
Lipton can get
together that kind of...


00:31:02.932 --> 00:31:04.351
money in the middle
of a recession, huh?


00:31:04.446 --> 00:31:06.998
It's what he does.
- So then what, he splits us up?


00:31:07.094 --> 00:31:10.106
Sell off the health care unit,
rail products, close Gloucester.


00:31:10.202 --> 00:31:11.698
He'll still have
consumer electronics...


00:31:11.794 --> 00:31:13.290
and the turbine and
defense departments.


00:31:13.386 --> 00:31:17.242
Whamo, we're a bargain.
You know, one more quarter,


00:31:17.338 --> 00:31:18.551
Lipton will be able
to put together enough


00:31:18.647 --> 00:31:19.620
Gloucester weight
to proxy battle.


00:31:19.716 --> 00:31:22.363
Install his own damn board.


00:31:23.630 --> 00:31:25.643
Jim's not gonna give up
without a fight, though.


00:31:25.739 --> 00:31:27.524
I'm sure he's already got
somebody out there looking for


00:31:27.620 --> 00:31:30.511
a white knight.
Keets, maybe Roberts,


00:31:30.607 --> 00:31:32.704
somebody with deep pockets.


00:31:32.799 --> 00:31:34.275
What?


00:31:34.371 --> 00:31:36.289
Nothing.


00:31:37.710 --> 00:31:41.010
Tell me more about
capital depreciations...


00:31:41.106 --> 00:31:43.062
of manufacturing assets.


00:31:50.256 --> 00:31:52.174
It's my office.


00:31:52.327 --> 00:31:54.457
I've got senior
staff at three-thirty.


00:31:54.552 --> 00:31:55.646
Reschedule.


00:31:55.742 --> 00:31:56.701
I can't.


00:31:56.797 --> 00:31:58.101
How about lunch
again next Tuesday?


00:31:58.197 --> 00:32:00.115
I don't think so.


00:32:38.366 --> 00:32:40.035
Hi, Jonas Geller, please.


00:32:40.131 --> 00:32:41.379
Robert Walker.


00:32:41.474 --> 00:32:42.917
Nope, doesn't know me.


00:32:43.013 --> 00:32:45.675
Mike Talbot recommended
me from Unicore.


00:32:45.771 --> 00:32:47.982
He said Mr. Geller
may have an opening...


00:32:48.077 --> 00:32:49.626
for a senior sales associate.


00:32:49.722 --> 00:32:51.718
Okay, that's too bad.


00:32:52.177 --> 00:32:54.211
It's okay, not the
first time I've heard it.


00:32:54.307 --> 00:32:55.266
Bye-bye.


00:32:55.362 --> 00:32:56.879
Sixty-five dollars
an hour for...


00:32:56.974 --> 00:32:58.729
oil rig workers in
the North Atlantic.


00:32:58.824 --> 00:33:00.530
Another thousand a
week if you've got...


00:33:00.626 --> 00:33:02.287
your commercial deep
sea certification!


00:33:02.382 --> 00:33:04.771
Doesn't everybody?
- I got mine last year at the Y.


00:33:04.867 --> 00:33:06.584
Six of clubs on
the Seven of hearts.


00:33:06.680 --> 00:33:08.311
Sally Wilcox please...


00:33:08.407 --> 00:33:11.571
Construction, hazardous waste
removal, aircraft mechanic.


00:33:11.667 --> 00:33:13.452
Thank god I got
my Doctorate, huh?


00:33:13.548 --> 00:33:15.331
Hey, is she in? It's
Bob Walker calling.


00:33:15.427 --> 00:33:17.490
He's calling her again.
- Hi, Sally.


00:33:17.586 --> 00:33:21.010
Bob Walker. Thanks for not
return any of my phone calls.


00:33:21.106 --> 00:33:22.819
If you do return my
call, I would love...


00:33:22.915 --> 00:33:23.897
to know why you fired me


00:33:23.993 --> 00:33:27.824
without any notice, you
fucking cowardly bitch.


00:33:28.089 --> 00:33:31.594
Gee, I wonder why she
never calls you back?


00:33:32.040 --> 00:33:33.958
It feels good, though.


00:33:34.533 --> 00:33:37.315
You know what I think?
It's quitting time.


00:33:37.410 --> 00:33:39.636
Quitting time? It's 3:30!


00:33:40.749 --> 00:33:42.840
A man can only take
so much rejection.


00:33:42.935 --> 00:33:45.104
I'm thirsty. Who's
coming? Conal?


00:33:45.200 --> 00:33:47.697
Sure, why not?
- I'm in.


00:33:47.793 --> 00:33:49.711
Alright, why not?


00:33:50.725 --> 00:33:54.801
I know... if you two are
going, it's gonna be good!


00:33:56.326 --> 00:33:57.457
Lipton bought how much?


00:33:57.553 --> 00:33:59.836
SEC filing says 3.8 percent.


00:34:00.355 --> 00:34:01.259
Hard hats gentlemen.


00:34:01.355 --> 00:34:03.020
He's just trying
to goose our stock.


00:34:03.116 --> 00:34:06.086
He gets it up ten a share,
he walks away with...


00:34:06.182 --> 00:34:08.335
a couple hundred
million in profit.


00:34:08.431 --> 00:34:10.168
Lipton wants more
than a couple...


00:34:10.264 --> 00:34:12.212
hundred million, he
wants the company.


00:34:12.308 --> 00:34:14.146
Well, our share price
is still too low.


00:34:14.242 --> 00:34:16.755
It's making us a
very tempting target.


00:34:16.851 --> 00:34:20.783
Paul, your office is over there.
- Whole floor legal?


00:34:20.879 --> 00:34:22.971
No. This is just
for the five of us.


00:34:23.066 --> 00:34:26.346
CFOs office. David,
Noah, you are over here.


00:34:26.442 --> 00:34:29.042
Conference rooms.
Private dining rooms.


00:34:29.138 --> 00:34:31.603
Bathrooms with
showers. Gym, kitchen.


00:34:31.699 --> 00:34:33.617
Gene! Come here.


00:34:35.688 --> 00:34:37.607
This is you.


00:34:39.334 --> 00:34:40.873
Well, don't get too excited,


00:34:40.969 --> 00:34:43.074
my office is gooing
to be much bigger.


00:34:43.170 --> 00:34:44.907
Well, what do you think?
- It's beautiful!


00:34:45.003 --> 00:34:45.703
This is amazing!


00:34:45.799 --> 00:34:49.307
(muffled) floor to
ceiling glass. Heck, if...


00:34:49.403 --> 00:34:53.723
you look that way, you can
see all the way to Boston.


00:35:16.548 --> 00:35:18.332
Hey, help me.


00:35:18.428 --> 00:35:20.629
Help? You need Help?
- Yeah.


00:35:21.613 --> 00:35:24.367
How you doing?
- You smell like a brewery.


00:35:24.463 --> 00:35:25.967
How does that happen?


00:35:26.063 --> 00:35:27.981
What's Drew doing?


00:35:28.326 --> 00:35:30.706
Waiting for you.
- Me? Why?


00:35:32.585 --> 00:35:35.112
I think he's worried about you.


00:35:47.663 --> 00:35:49.773
Wait up!
- Okay.


00:35:55.644 --> 00:35:58.089
What's going on out here, bud?


00:35:59.556 --> 00:36:02.328
I'm not a baby, I
can handle stuff.


00:36:25.262 --> 00:36:27.180
I lost my job.


00:36:31.284 --> 00:36:34.871
What'd you think it was?
- You and mom maybe.


00:36:36.311 --> 00:36:38.229
Me and mom are alright.


00:36:39.226 --> 00:36:41.672
You'll get another one, right?


00:36:42.565 --> 00:36:44.483
Yeah.


00:36:45.480 --> 00:36:50.113
Hey, you don't have to
worry about me, okay?


00:36:50.209 --> 00:36:52.271
Hey, look at me.


00:36:53.845 --> 00:36:57.221
You don't have to
worry about me, alright?


00:36:57.317 --> 00:36:59.235
I'm your dad.


00:37:00.213 --> 00:37:04.012
I'm gonna be fine, okay?


00:37:04.625 --> 00:37:06.331
Billionare investor
Arthur Lipton today...


00:37:06.426 --> 00:37:08.174
stepped up his campaign
for changes at GTX,


00:37:08.270 --> 00:37:11.089
Issuing a letter to
shareholders accusing executives


00:37:11.185 --> 00:37:12.548
of mismanagement,
and demanding new-


00:37:12.644 --> 00:37:15.660
What does it all mean?
- Nothing good.


00:37:17.823 --> 00:37:19.861
You need something, Phil?


00:37:20.930 --> 00:37:22.964
We lost Royal Caribbean.


00:37:39.538 --> 00:37:41.629
Do we have any cranberry jelly?


00:37:41.725 --> 00:37:43.844
Let me help you with that.


00:37:44.218 --> 00:37:46.137
Okay.


00:37:48.823 --> 00:37:51.259
How's business, Jack?
- Business? Well, we...


00:37:51.355 --> 00:37:53.944
We've got a big renovation
in Roxbury, next to that


00:37:54.040 --> 00:37:57.820
house I did last year. Nice
bonus when I finish by September.


00:37:57.915 --> 00:38:00.116
If you finish by September.


00:38:00.677 --> 00:38:03.553
Whenever you're ready
to plumb the place,


00:38:03.649 --> 00:38:06.452
give me a call, got
a special on Kohler.


00:38:06.548 --> 00:38:08.332
How's work, Bobby?


00:38:08.427 --> 00:38:09.387
Great, Jack.


00:38:09.482 --> 00:38:12.476
Line up more dollar-a-day
Laotian preschoolers


00:38:12.571 --> 00:38:15.813
to stitch tennis shoes
for you in Bangkok?


00:38:15.909 --> 00:38:17.885
I'm in manufacturing, Jack.


00:38:17.980 --> 00:38:20.034
Dollar-a-day Laotian
preschoolers aren't tall enough to


00:38:20.130 --> 00:38:23.472
turn the screws on
a deisel engine, so...


00:38:23.736 --> 00:38:25.254
You know, I was
reading about your guy


00:38:25.350 --> 00:38:26.786
Salinger in the
Globe the other day.


00:38:26.882 --> 00:38:30.046
Do you read now? Good.
- When they use small words.


00:38:30.142 --> 00:38:32.831
Said he made seven
hundred times...


00:38:32.927 --> 00:38:36.106
what average GTX
worker made last year.


00:38:36.473 --> 00:38:38.313
What do you think?
Salinger working...


00:38:38.409 --> 00:38:40.348
seven hundred times
harder than a welder


00:38:40.444 --> 00:38:43.129
pounding hot rivets into
a tanker hold all day?


00:38:43.225 --> 00:38:46.894
Why don't we say Grace
so the kids can start?


00:38:48.213 --> 00:38:50.496
Carson, would do the honors?


00:38:51.244 --> 00:38:55.675
Dear God, thank you for the food
and for letting us be together


00:38:55.770 --> 00:38:58.054
on Thanksgiving, and
everbody being okay.


00:38:58.150 --> 00:39:00.404
And please help
my dad find a job


00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:02.787
so he won't be
unhappy all the time.


00:39:02.883 --> 00:39:04.801
Amen.


00:39:06.283 --> 00:39:08.201
Okay.


00:39:10.427 --> 00:39:12.383
It's a nice table, Fran.


00:39:13.150 --> 00:39:15.068
Thank you.


00:39:23.164 --> 00:39:26.036
You know, if things
get tough, I could...


00:39:26.132 --> 00:39:28.861
always use some extra
help this winter.


00:39:28.957 --> 00:39:30.587
Hanging drywall?


00:39:30.683 --> 00:39:32.448
Yeah, there'll be lots
of work. We've got...


00:39:32.544 --> 00:39:34.597
four thousand square feet,
we're gutting the place-


00:39:34.693 --> 00:39:37.612
Thanks Jack, I
don't exactly see...


00:39:37.708 --> 00:39:40.966
myself pounding
nails, though. Ya know.


00:39:42.079 --> 00:39:43.997
Appreciate it.


00:39:51.862 --> 00:39:54.087
Your husband's such a dick.


00:39:58.366 --> 00:40:00.876
Goldman Sachs is doing due
diligence for Lipton and


00:40:00.972 --> 00:40:03.882
Skadden Arps is snooping around
for somebody, maybe Allied,


00:40:03.978 --> 00:40:06.153
maybe Siminov's Baltic
Global out of Moscow.


00:40:06.249 --> 00:40:07.605
What's the top
price Bater'll pay?


00:40:07.701 --> 00:40:09.759
Well, Lipton's put the
market value at one hundred-


00:40:09.855 --> 00:40:13.442
Alright, so we need to
get the stock to 102.


00:40:13.846 --> 00:40:16.589
That's seventeen more a share.
- Yeah, I can add Noah.


00:40:16.685 --> 00:40:18.737
We're already in danger
of missing our quarterly.


00:40:18.833 --> 00:40:21.144
We start fooling around
and miss our numbers again-


00:40:21.240 --> 00:40:22.920
No, we don't need to get
the stock to a hundred. We...


00:40:23.016 --> 00:40:24.761
get it in the mid-nineties,
it'll show a positive trend.


00:40:24.857 --> 00:40:29.014
How are we supposed to
boost the share price again?


00:40:31.416 --> 00:40:33.470
Increased efficiencies,
lowering costs.


00:40:33.566 --> 00:40:34.763
More downsizing,
suppose we try that...


00:40:34.858 --> 00:40:36.184
stunt again and the
stock stalls at ninety?


00:40:36.280 --> 00:40:38.188
Increasing market
value isn't a "stunt".


00:40:38.284 --> 00:40:39.446
We should at least
consider alternatives.


00:40:39.541 --> 00:40:40.644
How about selling
the Healthcare group?


00:40:40.740 --> 00:40:42.658
What!


00:40:42.850 --> 00:40:43.783
Maybe Lipton's right.


00:40:43.879 --> 00:40:45.420
Gene, c'mon,
healthcare's the only


00:40:45.516 --> 00:40:47.166
division that's
exhibiting any growth!


00:40:47.262 --> 00:40:49.315
I'm not breaking up the company.


00:40:49.411 --> 00:40:53.036
All right, how about selling
the new headquarters building?


00:40:53.132 --> 00:40:54.529
We're gonna need that space.


00:40:54.625 --> 00:40:56.643
Not if we keep firing
people, we're not.


00:40:56.739 --> 00:40:59.429
I'm not selling
the new building!


00:41:06.982 --> 00:41:08.583
Get a hold of Human
Resources, have...


00:41:08.679 --> 00:41:09.802
them start making up a list


00:41:09.898 --> 00:41:12.507
for another round of downsizing.


00:41:15.537 --> 00:41:18.309
Jim... Jim...!
Wait a minute, Jim!


00:41:18.952 --> 00:41:21.561
Could you guys give us a minute?


00:41:24.016 --> 00:41:26.491
What do you want me to do,
parrot back everything you say?


00:41:26.587 --> 00:41:28.781
I've always told
you what I thought,


00:41:28.877 --> 00:41:31.134
right or wrong. And
this... is wrong.


00:41:31.230 --> 00:41:33.148
I'm late for a meeting.


00:41:33.493 --> 00:41:37.977
We're not gonna be able to
make the mortgage next month.


00:41:39.478 --> 00:41:44.485
I talked to Bridget. She thinks
if we price the house low enough,


00:41:44.581 --> 00:41:47.431
we might be able
to get as much as...


00:41:47.527 --> 00:41:50.788
eight hundred and
fifty thousand for it.


00:41:51.563 --> 00:41:54.253
That's less than
we've got in it.


00:41:54.939 --> 00:41:58.852
Yeah... it doesn't matter
how much we got in it.


00:41:59.122 --> 00:42:01.975
Your severance
ends in three weeks.


00:42:02.881 --> 00:42:04.396
We're going to end
up in foreclosure.


00:42:04.492 --> 00:42:08.502
We won't have enough money
to put down on another house.


00:42:08.598 --> 00:42:11.012
We're not going to be
able to qualify for...


00:42:11.108 --> 00:42:13.298
another house on just
my salary, anyway.


00:42:13.394 --> 00:42:15.312
Okay.


00:42:15.426 --> 00:42:18.976
So where we gonna end up? We
gonna pitch a tent in the park?


00:42:19.072 --> 00:42:20.990
Yeah.
- Okay.


00:42:24.405 --> 00:42:26.932
We can move in with your folks.


00:42:27.090 --> 00:42:29.862
No. - They have
two extra bedrooms-


00:42:30.313 --> 00:42:32.633
Maggie, we're not
living with my parents.


00:42:32.729 --> 00:42:34.647
It'd just be temporary.


00:42:35.722 --> 00:42:38.485
I choose death. I opt for death.


00:42:39.367 --> 00:42:42.138
No, I'd have to
kill myself first.


00:42:45.122 --> 00:42:46.730
Jack said he offered
you a job the...


00:42:46.826 --> 00:42:48.748
other day and you shut
him down pretty hard.


00:42:48.844 --> 00:42:52.838
Can you imagine that? Me
working for your brother?


00:42:55.289 --> 00:42:57.490
He was just trying to help.


00:42:57.667 --> 00:42:59.682
How? By letting me hang drywall?


00:42:59.778 --> 00:43:02.061
Well, you'd get back
into great shape.


00:43:02.156 --> 00:43:06.875
Callouses, a tan.
- In the middle of winter?


00:43:07.028 --> 00:43:09.035
Big, broad shoulders...


00:43:09.131 --> 00:43:12.477
from carrying all
that heavy lumber...


00:43:13.819 --> 00:43:16.020
I gotta get up early, baby.


00:43:33.309 --> 00:43:36.488
Bobby Walker keeps
leaving me messages.


00:43:37.146 --> 00:43:38.999
My assistant thinks
he's psychotic,


00:43:39.095 --> 00:43:41.001
wants me to get a
restraining order.


00:43:41.097 --> 00:43:43.461
I'm sure you've gotten worse.


00:43:46.968 --> 00:43:48.913
So what do you think?
You gonna get away...


00:43:49.008 --> 00:43:50.861
for a day or two for
skiing at Christmas?


00:43:50.957 --> 00:43:53.484
I don't know, I'll have to see.


00:43:53.989 --> 00:43:57.902
Did Hansen get you started
on that new list yet?


00:43:59.590 --> 00:44:01.872
I was at the meeting, Sally.


00:44:02.621 --> 00:44:04.769
Yesterday.
- How many?


00:44:06.113 --> 00:44:08.151
How many?
- Five thousand.


00:44:09.105 --> 00:44:12.232
Well, what is the criteria
for getting canned this time?


00:44:12.328 --> 00:44:15.148
Gary Hunt's put on a few pounds,
maybe we should let him go.


00:44:15.244 --> 00:44:17.832
And I hear Jill
Carter has cancer.


00:44:17.928 --> 00:44:21.841
We could save a bundle
on her insurance premiums!


00:44:25.218 --> 00:44:27.136
Sally.


00:44:30.283 --> 00:44:34.216
Ho, the billionare boy's
club, how's the plotting going?


00:44:34.312 --> 00:44:36.863
Warren Buffet still safe on
top of the Fortune 500 list?


00:44:36.959 --> 00:44:38.202
How's the job
search going, Bobby?


00:44:38.298 --> 00:44:39.884
Good, actually, not
bad. They're out there.


00:44:39.980 --> 00:44:42.502
Mr. Conners, your
group's on the first tee.


00:44:42.598 --> 00:44:43.878
Ready to get your
ass kicked, Eric?


00:44:43.974 --> 00:44:44.267
Let's go!


00:44:44.363 --> 00:44:46.070
...Mr. Walker?


00:44:46.166 --> 00:44:48.775
Can I speak to you for a moment?


00:44:51.768 --> 00:44:54.338
Hey, what the hell's going on?


00:44:55.259 --> 00:44:56.716
I just got thrown off
the course at the club.


00:44:56.812 --> 00:44:57.466
Keep your voice down.


00:44:57.562 --> 00:44:59.691
We haven't paid the
dues since October?


00:44:59.787 --> 00:45:02.791
I haven't been paying
a lot of things.


00:45:02.887 --> 00:45:05.414
I look like a fucking deadbeat!


00:45:05.426 --> 00:45:08.667
This is real, Bobby.
This is happening. To us.


00:45:08.763 --> 00:45:11.692
You're wandering around like
you're in some sort of a daze.


00:45:11.788 --> 00:45:14.615
What, you're playing golf?
Getting your Porsche detailed?


00:45:14.711 --> 00:45:18.087
Maggie, I need to
look successful. Okay?


00:45:19.391 --> 00:45:21.933
I can't just look like
another asshole with resume.


00:45:22.029 --> 00:45:25.371
You are just another
asshole with resume!


00:45:30.325 --> 00:45:31.774
I cut them a check
for the balance.


00:45:31.870 --> 00:45:33.788
Cancel it.
- No.


00:45:36.656 --> 00:45:38.804
We can't afford it.
- No.


00:46:06.427 --> 00:46:08.019
I should've been honest
with you about the club,


00:46:08.115 --> 00:46:10.169
but you haven't
been honest with me.


00:46:10.265 --> 00:46:12.121
We're not going to
need these, are we?


00:46:12.217 --> 00:46:14.273
I thought we'd have
a little rummage sale-


00:46:14.369 --> 00:46:18.666
You need to get a job, any job.


00:46:21.927 --> 00:46:24.056
I can't do this alone, Bobby.


00:46:24.152 --> 00:46:25.546
I know. I'm out there
playing golf. In two...


00:46:25.642 --> 00:46:26.972
weeks I won't be able
to support my family.


00:46:27.068 --> 00:46:29.121
Things are going
to get great again.


00:46:29.217 --> 00:46:31.078
No.
- We can get through this!


00:46:31.174 --> 00:46:34.415
Things aren't going to
be great again. Okay?


00:46:34.511 --> 00:46:38.367
I'm trying to get a job.
I've been out there every day.


00:46:38.463 --> 00:46:41.479
For three months
trying to get a job.


00:46:41.686 --> 00:46:44.256
I haven't had one offer.


00:46:44.640 --> 00:46:46.463
I've been to everybody we know.


00:46:46.558 --> 00:46:50.342
And a lot of people I
don't. And I have begged.


00:46:50.438 --> 00:46:52.356
I've fucking begged!


00:46:52.736 --> 00:46:54.654
For a lead, anything.


00:46:56.035 --> 00:46:58.480
There's thousands of
new MBAs out there.


00:46:58.576 --> 00:47:01.167
No mortgage, no kids, work
ninety hour work weeks.


00:47:01.262 --> 00:47:02.883
For nothing.


00:47:02.979 --> 00:47:04.258
You want honesty, Maggie?


00:47:04.354 --> 00:47:06.644
I'm a thirty-seven year
old unemployed loser


00:47:06.739 --> 00:47:09.104
who can't support his family.


00:47:09.366 --> 00:47:12.627
Okay, look. You are
going to find a job.


00:47:12.820 --> 00:47:17.156
Working for people who know
how lucky they are to have you.


00:47:17.252 --> 00:47:19.966
When did it all go to shit?
- It hasn't turned to shit.


00:47:20.062 --> 00:47:24.137
You have Drew, and Carson,
and your parents and me.


00:47:26.036 --> 00:47:28.032
Okay? You have me.


00:47:41.229 --> 00:47:43.052
We're still at least
seventy-five short.


00:47:43.148 --> 00:47:44.633
What about Debra Hayes,
Senior Director...


00:47:44.729 --> 00:47:45.776
of Accounting, Maritime Sales?


00:47:45.872 --> 00:47:47.526
Debra Hayes has ten
years with the...


00:47:47.621 --> 00:47:49.229
company and
outstanding evaluations.


00:47:49.325 --> 00:47:51.109
She also has a husband with
a successful law practice


00:47:51.204 --> 00:47:52.294
and two kids who would be...


00:47:52.390 --> 00:47:53.641
delighted to have mommy at home.


00:47:53.737 --> 00:47:55.981
She's sixty, I doubt her
kids are still living at home,


00:47:56.077 --> 00:47:57.756
much less calling her "Mommy. "


00:47:57.852 --> 00:48:00.010
Phil Woodward's
back on this list.


00:48:00.106 --> 00:48:02.656
He fits the criteria.
- Wasn't talking to you, Dick.


00:48:02.752 --> 00:48:03.622
He's grossly overpaid
and just blew...


00:48:03.718 --> 00:48:04.540
a five hundred
million dollar deal-


00:48:04.636 --> 00:48:05.573
What are you, deaf?
Shut the fuck up!


00:48:05.669 --> 00:48:06.789
This list is still
preliminary, Gene.


00:48:06.885 --> 00:48:08.604
I'm looking and all I see
are people who are over fifty,


00:48:08.700 --> 00:48:10.295
with just enough
young ones thrown...


00:48:10.391 --> 00:48:11.942
in to protect us
against litigation.


00:48:12.038 --> 00:48:13.515
I'm confident all of
these dismissals...


00:48:13.610 --> 00:48:15.087
will stand up to
outside legal scrutiny.


00:48:15.183 --> 00:48:17.466
What about ethical scrutiny?


00:48:18.214 --> 00:48:20.985
We're not breaking
any laws, Gene.


00:48:21.245 --> 00:48:23.734
I guess I always
assumed we were trying...


00:48:23.830 --> 00:48:25.715
for a higher standard than that,


00:48:25.811 --> 00:48:27.729
Paul.


00:48:41.120 --> 00:48:44.304
Mr. Walker? Troy Thayer.


00:48:45.607 --> 00:48:47.046
Have a seat.


00:48:47.142 --> 00:48:49.425
Thanks for seeing me.
- Sure.


00:48:49.521 --> 00:48:51.517
A GTX casualty.
- Yeah.


00:48:52.092 --> 00:48:54.864
How you holding up?
- Good, thanks.


00:48:55.084 --> 00:48:57.482
Dan Mass gave you a
great recommendation.


00:48:57.578 --> 00:49:00.090
MBA. You went to
school at State college?


00:49:00.186 --> 00:49:02.470
Undergrad, yeah.
- My wife went to Penn.


00:49:02.566 --> 00:49:04.484
Really?
- Loved it.


00:49:05.097 --> 00:49:08.146
You willing to work
for ninety a year,


00:49:08.242 --> 00:49:10.362
plus commission and bonus?


00:49:11.197 --> 00:49:12.521
Ah... yeah.


00:49:12.617 --> 00:49:13.864
Well, the good news is
that we're growing fast,


00:49:13.960 --> 00:49:16.281
and there's plenty of
head room around here.


00:49:16.377 --> 00:49:19.351
So, I can't promise you anything,
but with Dan's recommendation


00:49:19.447 --> 00:49:22.305
and your resume, you seem
like the right fit for the job.


00:49:22.401 --> 00:49:24.319
Thanks.


00:49:26.774 --> 00:49:28.098
Ho!


00:49:28.194 --> 00:49:29.901
Who's winning?
- Who knows?


00:49:29.997 --> 00:49:31.704
Hey, how'd it go?
- The interview?


00:49:31.800 --> 00:49:33.718
It was good. Good.


00:49:36.596 --> 00:49:38.027
Yeah, we're getting
our asses kicked.


00:49:38.123 --> 00:49:38.954
You can take my place.


00:49:39.050 --> 00:49:41.430
Blue! Thirty-two!


00:50:08.286 --> 00:50:10.487
Bob Walker for Troy Thayer.


00:50:11.393 --> 00:50:13.504
That's okay.


00:50:14.079 --> 00:50:18.237
I'm actually just calling
in regards to a position.


00:50:18.836 --> 00:50:20.754
Sure,


00:50:20.984 --> 00:50:23.675
Northeast Regional
Sales Manager.


00:50:28.697 --> 00:50:30.615
It has.


00:50:33.415 --> 00:50:35.334
Thank you very much.


00:50:50.795 --> 00:50:53.749
What's that?
- My last pay check.


00:51:31.770 --> 00:51:34.008
So at the end of this hour
long rant we all turn...


00:51:34.104 --> 00:51:36.431
to the translator and the
guy says, "Mr. Lan say no. "


00:51:36.527 --> 00:51:37.804
This guy kept babbling
on and on and on.


00:51:37.899 --> 00:51:39.913
Mr. Lin said... wait,
you were at a banquet


00:51:40.009 --> 00:51:41.198
with nine meat soup?


00:51:41.293 --> 00:51:43.059
Yeah. I didn't know they
had nine meats in China.


00:51:43.155 --> 00:51:44.555
I didn't either,
can you name them?


00:51:44.651 --> 00:51:45.976
Well, beef, pork,
chicken, shark fin-


00:51:46.072 --> 00:51:46.205
Gene.


00:51:46.301 --> 00:51:47.912
Hey Phil, grab a drink.


00:51:48.008 --> 00:51:48.967
Gene!


00:51:49.063 --> 00:51:51.039
Relax, Phil. Grab a
drink man, is a party.


00:51:51.135 --> 00:51:53.447
Sally Wilcox just fired me.


00:51:57.053 --> 00:51:59.345
Find Sally Wilcox and tell her
to get her ass up here right now!


00:51:59.441 --> 00:52:01.805
She's already in your office.


00:52:09.868 --> 00:52:11.825
You fired Phil Woodward.


00:52:12.362 --> 00:52:14.726
Hire him back.
- Gene, please.


00:52:14.769 --> 00:52:15.900
Goddam Sally, we
talked about this.


00:52:15.996 --> 00:52:17.914
Gene!


00:52:47.427 --> 00:52:49.346
You too?


00:52:57.518 --> 00:52:59.436
Ah, fuck 'em!


00:53:03.886 --> 00:53:06.189
They think this is tough?


00:53:10.408 --> 00:53:14.566
I worked hull assembly at
Gloucester, remember Gene?


00:53:17.046 --> 00:53:20.671
Try spot-welding inside a
thirty-six inch propeller shaft,


00:53:20.767 --> 00:53:22.724
sixty hours a week.


00:54:58.446 --> 00:55:01.804
You will never guess
who's in Joanna's office.


00:55:01.900 --> 00:55:05.478
Gene McClary's favorite
ass-kisser, Phil Woodward.


00:55:05.574 --> 00:55:08.162
Your resume's very
impressive, Phil.


00:55:08.258 --> 00:55:10.176
Thank you.


00:55:10.570 --> 00:55:11.770
You started on
the factory floor,


00:55:11.866 --> 00:55:14.657
not many people can
claim that any more.


00:55:14.753 --> 00:55:17.345
You want to get rid
of all the ancient...


00:55:17.441 --> 00:55:19.260
stuff, anything pre-nineties.


00:55:19.356 --> 00:55:20.621
Instead of listing
the number of years...


00:55:20.717 --> 00:55:21.630
you held each position at GTX,


00:55:21.726 --> 00:55:24.008
indicate your title
and responsibilities.


00:55:24.104 --> 00:55:27.614
And here, where you've noted your
military service, don't say Vietnam.


00:55:27.710 --> 00:55:30.971
Combat infantryman
is impressive enough.


00:55:31.250 --> 00:55:35.134
You smoke, Phil?
- Occasionally.


00:55:35.230 --> 00:55:38.051
Quit. Employers don't want
employee health problems


00:55:38.147 --> 00:55:39.854
ratcheting up their
insurance premiums, Phil.


00:55:39.950 --> 00:55:41.667
And you might want to
think about dying your hair.


00:55:41.763 --> 00:55:42.846
Getting rid of some of the grey.


00:55:42.942 --> 00:55:44.985
Do we know each other?


00:55:45.905 --> 00:55:49.473
Excuse me?
- You keep using my first name.


00:55:51.698 --> 00:55:53.654
I'm not the enemy, Phil.


00:55:53.684 --> 00:55:56.561
You're pushing sixty
and you look like hell.


00:55:56.657 --> 00:56:00.244
You're going to have
a rough time out there.


00:56:09.500 --> 00:56:13.337
Could you show me
to my office, please?


00:56:20.013 --> 00:56:23.207
You got a window. Company
had to pay extra for that.


00:56:23.303 --> 00:56:25.498
Least the pricks could do.


00:56:27.878 --> 00:56:31.709
How's the best damn
salesman on the East Coast?


00:56:32.060 --> 00:56:36.050
Unemployed.
- Yes, lot of that going around.


00:56:40.231 --> 00:56:44.193
Dress code pretty
lax around here?


00:56:44.289 --> 00:56:46.734
You should see casual Fridays.


00:56:47.330 --> 00:56:49.899
Hello? Yeah.


00:56:52.278 --> 00:56:54.321
I talked with somebody else
from your company last week,


00:56:54.417 --> 00:56:56.565
and they said I wasn't
going to have to...


00:56:56.661 --> 00:56:58.705
make another payment
on that this month.


00:56:58.801 --> 00:57:01.803
Look, I don't know
what you want me to do.


00:57:01.899 --> 00:57:04.795
I can lie to you, tell you
I'm writing you a check,


00:57:04.891 --> 00:57:06.254
and I'm gonna put it in the mail,
and you'll have it right away.


00:57:06.350 --> 00:57:08.778
Okay? I'm going to write
you a check right now,


00:57:08.874 --> 00:57:10.512
I'm going to put it in the mail,


00:57:10.608 --> 00:57:12.334
and you'll have it
tomorrow, how's that sound?


00:57:12.430 --> 00:57:15.854
Terrific, outstanding!
Look forward to it.


00:57:17.025 --> 00:57:19.528
Which one, American Express?


00:57:19.624 --> 00:57:21.542
The mortgage.


00:57:22.857 --> 00:57:25.091
Yvette asked me if I
could work tomorrow night.


00:57:25.187 --> 00:57:27.048
That's New Year's
Eve. - Double-time.


00:57:27.143 --> 00:57:28.390
Dad?
- Yeah?


00:57:28.486 --> 00:57:29.810
Can you drive me over to Kyle's?


00:57:29.905 --> 00:57:33.522
No, I'm busy now, okay? C'mon!


00:57:38.279 --> 00:57:41.819
C'mon Drew. Hey, why
don't you play Guitar Hero?


00:57:41.915 --> 00:57:44.312
Halo? Why don't
you play some Xbox?


00:57:44.408 --> 00:57:45.732
Okay Bobby, hang on a sec...


00:57:45.827 --> 00:57:51.323
Come here. Hey, Drew! Hey! Drew!


00:57:52.320 --> 00:57:56.627
Dammit, there's a fucking
Nor-Easter outside.


00:57:56.723 --> 00:57:58.383
Kid's pissed off because I
won't drive him to Cotuit...


00:57:58.479 --> 00:57:59.985
to visit the Matlock's,
right when he wants me to.


00:58:00.081 --> 00:58:01.233
We just bought him
the damn thing for


00:58:01.328 --> 00:58:02.642
Christmas, and he's
already bored with it?


00:58:02.738 --> 00:58:03.850
He doesn't have
the Xbox any more.


00:58:03.946 --> 00:58:05.577
Why? What happened to it?
- He gave it back.


00:58:05.673 --> 00:58:08.689
What?
- He knew we couldn't afford it.


00:58:09.778 --> 00:58:12.957
He asked me if he
could, and I said yes.


00:58:12.971 --> 00:58:15.877
He's right. We can't afford it.


00:58:50.560 --> 00:58:53.515
I need a job, Jack.


00:59:14.385 --> 00:59:18.461
Don't think you're gonna
be needing that just yet.


00:59:19.872 --> 00:59:21.790
Nice tool belt.


00:59:56.473 --> 00:59:58.391
Keep 'em coming, Bob.


01:00:00.885 --> 01:00:02.803
Hey, Bobby.


01:00:03.839 --> 01:00:06.563
Yeah?
- Grab two this time.


01:00:35.069 --> 01:00:37.409
Lunch.
- Oh, where we going?


01:00:54.444 --> 01:00:58.357
They're new. That's why
you're getting blisters.


01:00:58.510 --> 01:00:59.958
Thanks.


01:01:00.054 --> 01:01:03.268
Here.
- Appreciate it.


01:01:13.780 --> 01:01:16.878
Hey. You want to
come down for dinner?


01:01:17.924 --> 01:01:20.274
I want you to take
a gun and shoot me.


01:01:20.369 --> 01:01:21.846
Just shoot me.


01:01:21.942 --> 01:01:23.860
Oh, let me see.


01:01:24.101 --> 01:01:26.139
Let me get the neosporin.


01:01:26.480 --> 01:01:29.740
I hate your brother,
I fucking hate him.


01:01:31.160 --> 01:01:36.530
I don't think I can go back.
- Sure you can.


01:02:07.799 --> 01:02:10.897
Too thin, add another
sack to the mix.


01:02:17.967 --> 01:02:19.894
Easy work, huh Bobby?


01:02:19.990 --> 01:02:23.398
Pretty much like moving
cost reports from...


01:02:23.494 --> 01:02:26.591
the in-box to the
out-box, am I right?


01:02:29.514 --> 01:02:31.432
Didn't say nothing.


01:02:47.584 --> 01:02:50.111
What do you have planned today?


01:02:50.884 --> 01:02:52.802
Not much.


01:02:53.147 --> 01:02:56.408
Ed and Dana invited
us to dinner tonight.


01:02:57.214 --> 01:03:00.168
Who?
- My old friends.


01:03:01.895 --> 01:03:04.733
Seven thirty.


01:03:07.036 --> 01:03:11.275
Pick up a nice bottle of
Pinot when you go out, okay?


01:03:14.556 --> 01:03:16.474
Okay.


01:03:20.963 --> 01:03:23.159
Hi, Phil Woodward. I have an-


01:03:23.255 --> 01:03:25.619
Just sign in and take a seat.


01:03:46.437 --> 01:03:47.905
Hell Jack, you hear that?


01:03:48.001 --> 01:03:51.895
Bob gets twelve weeks pay, when
they fucking shit-canned him.


01:03:51.991 --> 01:03:55.539
My uncle Tommy worked for the
phone company nineteen years.


01:03:55.635 --> 01:03:59.770
They laid him off ten months
short of lifetime medical.


01:03:59.866 --> 01:04:03.223
They hire him back,
like four months later.


01:04:03.319 --> 01:04:06.580
Half his old wages, no benefits.


01:04:07.616 --> 01:04:10.306
What's this?
- It's your paycheck.


01:04:11.836 --> 01:04:15.903
Hey, Jack? There's an
extra two hundred in this.


01:04:21.696 --> 01:04:24.305
I must have made a mistake, Bob.


01:05:28.913 --> 01:05:31.099
You going to be alright
sleeping in the...


01:05:31.195 --> 01:05:33.114
same room as your
sister for a while?


01:05:33.210 --> 01:05:35.128
Sure.


01:05:47.444 --> 01:05:51.203
All tucked in?
- Yeah, Dad.


01:05:58.032 --> 01:06:01.374
I couldn't wait to
get out of this house.


01:06:02.483 --> 01:06:06.972
My parents, the
neighborhood, the church.


01:06:12.918 --> 01:06:15.757
I was going to be the CEO.


01:06:23.316 --> 01:06:26.587
She seems nice,
Dad. Good with kids.


01:06:26.683 --> 01:06:29.129
She have any of her own?
- Hey.


01:06:29.608 --> 01:06:31.650
What? Never too late to start.


01:06:31.746 --> 01:06:34.451
Think you and Susan could
get away for a week in June?


01:06:34.547 --> 01:06:36.370
We've rented a house
out on Stonewall Beach.


01:06:36.466 --> 01:06:38.739
June? Maybe...


01:06:41.002 --> 01:06:42.585
So, you keeping busy?


01:06:42.681 --> 01:06:47.276
Yeah, I've been asked join a
couple boards. Dynex, Procar.


01:06:47.371 --> 01:06:50.920
You going to do it?
- I don't know, I think I'm...


01:06:51.016 --> 01:06:53.706
I think I'm tired
of board rooms.


01:06:54.392 --> 01:06:56.627
Why don't you start
a consulting firm?


01:06:56.723 --> 01:06:57.930
Yeah?
- Sure.


01:06:58.026 --> 01:07:01.776
There is always somebody
out there willing to...


01:07:01.872 --> 01:07:06.274
pay an opinionated old
bastard for some shitty advice.


01:07:09.163 --> 01:07:11.693
So what do you say to
the Vineyard in June?


01:07:11.789 --> 01:07:13.239
Your mother will be okay.


01:07:13.335 --> 01:07:15.253
You two talking?


01:07:17.680 --> 01:07:20.322
She's having a
pretty rough time.


01:07:20.418 --> 01:07:23.516
She's talking about
selling the house.


01:07:24.011 --> 01:07:26.619
Look Daddy, I found another egg!


01:07:34.292 --> 01:07:38.331
Where's Mike?
- He got busted again.


01:07:38.427 --> 01:07:39.232
For what?


01:07:39.327 --> 01:07:42.004
Drunk and disorderly, assault.


01:07:43.654 --> 01:07:46.704
He managed to take a swing
at one of the cops, too.


01:07:46.800 --> 01:07:48.718
Nice.


01:07:50.098 --> 01:07:51.413
Bobby?
- Yeah.


01:07:51.509 --> 01:07:54.525
You still have your tool belt?
- Yeah.


01:07:54.971 --> 01:07:58.540
Why don't you grab it.
- Alright!


01:08:05.216 --> 01:08:07.286
Oh, Jesus!


01:08:08.055 --> 01:08:09.790
I thought I had
it measured right.


01:08:09.886 --> 01:08:12.898
You gotta rip out all this
shit before Jack sees it.


01:08:12.994 --> 01:08:15.765
The whole thing?
- Yeah, all of it.


01:08:16.265 --> 01:08:18.237
Use your speed
square as a spacer.


01:08:18.333 --> 01:08:19.650
Get it on two points...


01:08:19.746 --> 01:08:21.223
Gimme that!


01:08:21.319 --> 01:08:23.237
Alright?


01:08:26.700 --> 01:08:29.952
You got it?
- Yeah.


01:08:39.169 --> 01:08:42.022
You finally done?
- That side, yeah.


01:08:44.924 --> 01:08:48.338
Jesus Christ, that's ugly.


01:08:51.983 --> 01:08:56.874
If you need another guy, I know
somebody who could use a job.


01:08:57.278 --> 01:09:02.687
Yeah? Well whoever it is, let's
hope he isn't as slow as you are.


01:09:04.797 --> 01:09:06.715
Okay.


01:09:41.169 --> 01:09:43.968
He ever sing on key?
- Nope.


01:10:09.367 --> 01:10:12.177
What're you doing?


01:10:12.273 --> 01:10:14.191
Ah, getting drunk.


01:10:15.698 --> 01:10:17.472
I called outplacement, to see
if you wanted to have lunch.


01:10:17.568 --> 01:10:19.256
They said you haven't
been coming in much lately.


01:10:19.352 --> 01:10:22.613
Oh, yeah?
- A couple of weeks now.


01:10:22.709 --> 01:10:24.637
No kidding?


01:10:28.780 --> 01:10:30.698
Miss?


01:10:33.308 --> 01:10:35.552
What'd you say I
give you a ride home?


01:10:35.648 --> 01:10:38.910
Can't go home.


01:10:40.980 --> 01:10:44.405
Lorna doesn't want the neighbors
to know that I got fired,


01:10:44.501 --> 01:10:47.354
so I can't show
up until after six.


01:10:49.037 --> 01:10:52.868
Makes me haul my briefcase
back and forth, too.


01:10:53.526 --> 01:10:56.519
You see the Journal
this morning?


01:10:58.015 --> 01:11:01.622
They listed how much
CEOs made last year.


01:11:02.849 --> 01:11:05.554
Know who was
seventeenth on the list?


01:11:05.650 --> 01:11:08.374
James Salinger, GTX.


01:11:12.901 --> 01:11:14.939
Want to go to the movies?


01:11:15.664 --> 01:11:17.476
Take you to a matinee. I'm
sure they still have matinees.


01:11:17.572 --> 01:11:22.219
We can get a bucket of popcorn,
couple of those big colas.


01:11:38.415 --> 01:11:40.333
Hey, Daddy.


01:11:40.794 --> 01:11:42.712
Hey, beautiful.


01:11:44.246 --> 01:11:45.675
What're you smiling at?


01:11:45.771 --> 01:11:48.754
A man called today from
Chicago. Fred Munder?


01:11:48.850 --> 01:11:50.360
He said he was
impressed with your...


01:11:50.456 --> 01:11:51.966
resume, wants you
to give him a call.


01:11:52.062 --> 01:11:54.508
His phone number's over there.


01:11:55.065 --> 01:11:57.415
Detroit is where he's based,
the guy's a headhunter.


01:11:57.511 --> 01:11:59.794
I just thought the
job was in Boston.


01:11:59.890 --> 01:12:03.323
It is in Boston. I'm going to go
there, I'm going to stay at Motel 6.


01:12:03.419 --> 01:12:06.047
Okay? I'm going to
eat very inexpensively.


01:12:06.143 --> 01:12:09.462
The job is a Vice-President
of Sales and Marketing


01:12:09.558 --> 01:12:13.039
with extensive experience
in transportation.


01:12:13.135 --> 01:12:15.792
This is it, this is
me, this is my job.


01:12:15.888 --> 01:12:20.290
I don't know what else I can
look for, this is the one!


01:13:14.732 --> 01:13:18.328
Excuse me, I have an appointment
with Frederick Munder,


01:13:18.424 --> 01:13:20.342
Robert Walker.


01:13:41.013 --> 01:13:43.296
Mr. Walker?
- Yes.


01:13:43.985 --> 01:13:46.182
I'm Jane Nefeld, Mr.
Munder's assistant.


01:13:46.278 --> 01:13:46.385
Hi.


01:13:46.481 --> 01:13:48.081
You say you have an appointment?


01:13:48.177 --> 01:13:50.699
Yes, at 10.
- I don't see it.


01:13:52.195 --> 01:13:57.644
I spoke to Mr. Munder
myself, so... Friday at 10.


01:13:58.986 --> 01:14:00.953
We talked two days ago.


01:14:01.049 --> 01:14:04.646
Oh, my. He has you down for
next Friday, the seventeeth.


01:14:04.742 --> 01:14:08.444
Can you come back next week?
- I flew in from Boston.


01:14:08.539 --> 01:14:09.498
Oh, I'm so sorry.


01:14:09.594 --> 01:14:11.484
I don't mind just sitting
in the waiting room.


01:14:11.580 --> 01:14:13.006
Or I can come back
this afternoon, my...


01:14:13.102 --> 01:14:14.343
flight doesn't
leave until tonight.


01:14:14.438 --> 01:14:16.799
Mr. Munder is in
Dallas on business.


01:14:16.895 --> 01:14:19.911
He won't be back
'til next Wednesday.


01:15:09.311 --> 01:15:11.488
Hey, sorry I'm late.
Got caught on a call.


01:15:11.584 --> 01:15:13.100
No problem, I got a drink.


01:15:13.196 --> 01:15:15.469
Looks good. I'll
have what he's having.


01:15:15.565 --> 01:15:17.513
Hang on, you know you want?


01:15:17.609 --> 01:15:19.973
I'll have the Cobb, no bacon.


01:15:22.241 --> 01:15:25.420
Ah... rib-eye,
medium-rare, with fries.


01:15:27.688 --> 01:15:29.398
Sorry to rush things,
I have to get...


01:15:29.494 --> 01:15:31.343
back for a staff a
meeting at one thirty.


01:15:31.439 --> 01:15:32.992
You look great,
you losing weight?


01:15:33.088 --> 01:15:37.279
Oh yeah, well, dying my hair.


01:15:39.429 --> 01:15:42.048
So how are you doing?
- I'm fine,


01:15:42.144 --> 01:15:44.694
sending out a lot of resumes.


01:15:44.790 --> 01:15:47.154
You're lucky to be out of it.


01:15:47.831 --> 01:15:51.773
Word on the street is you're
looking for a foreign exec.


01:15:51.869 --> 01:15:53.998
You have someone to recommend?


01:15:54.094 --> 01:15:56.012
Yeah, me.


01:15:57.192 --> 01:15:58.966
It's international, all travel.


01:15:59.062 --> 01:16:02.380
I have extensive
overseas experience.


01:16:02.476 --> 01:16:04.394
I'm sure you do.


01:16:05.019 --> 01:16:08.361
You mind my asking,
how old are you, Phil?


01:16:11.157 --> 01:16:13.881
You're not worried I'll sue?


01:16:15.684 --> 01:16:17.880
I wouldn't hire anyone
over thirty for that job.


01:16:17.976 --> 01:16:18.954
It's a killer.


01:16:19.050 --> 01:16:22.882
Out of the country five
out of every six weeks.


01:16:23.780 --> 01:16:26.359
Travel's not a problem.


01:16:26.455 --> 01:16:28.650
Why don't you cash
it in? Shit, I would.


01:16:28.746 --> 01:16:29.707
Go lie on a beach.


01:16:29.803 --> 01:16:33.390
I can't afford to go
lie on a fucking beach.


01:16:37.897 --> 01:16:39.634
I can't recommend
you for the job, Phil.


01:16:39.730 --> 01:16:42.502
They'd laugh me
out of the office.


01:17:06.020 --> 01:17:08.662
Lorna's pretty
worried about you,


01:17:08.758 --> 01:17:12.019
has you wrapped around
a tree someplace.


01:17:12.056 --> 01:17:14.461
Sons of bitches!


01:17:21.059 --> 01:17:22.978
Motherfuckers!


01:17:25.165 --> 01:17:28.028
Tom Brady couldn't
hit that building...


01:17:28.124 --> 01:17:30.017
from here on his best day.


01:17:30.113 --> 01:17:33.528
Sarah's tuition
for Brown is due.


01:17:34.296 --> 01:17:36.953
I write the check, I
can't make the mortgage.


01:17:37.049 --> 01:17:40.741
Hell, I could...
- No, you stop it.


01:17:47.379 --> 01:17:49.719
You know the worst part?


01:17:51.100 --> 01:17:53.018
The world didn't stop.


01:17:54.668 --> 01:17:57.299
The newspaper still
came every morning,


01:17:57.395 --> 01:18:00.164
the automatic sprinklers
shut off at six,


01:18:00.260 --> 01:18:04.374
Jeff next door still
washed his car every Sunday.


01:18:08.096 --> 01:18:09.794
My life ended,


01:18:09.890 --> 01:18:13.621
and nobody noticed.


01:18:25.246 --> 01:18:26.943
Hey, Bobby.
- Yeah.


01:18:27.039 --> 01:18:30.218
Boss says it's quitting time.
- Alright.


01:18:39.824 --> 01:18:40.831
Where's Jack?


01:18:40.927 --> 01:18:43.780
Still working.
Come on, I'm buying.


01:18:43.815 --> 01:18:44.291
What's he doing?


01:18:44.387 --> 01:18:46.011
He's working late, to make
the completion deadline.


01:18:46.107 --> 01:18:48.697
To get the bonus.
- He doesn't want our help?


01:18:48.793 --> 01:18:52.950
He can't pay us.
- He could pay us out of the bonus.


01:18:54.595 --> 01:18:56.831
He needs the bonus
to break even.


01:18:56.927 --> 01:19:02.144
He underbid to get the job to
keep us working through the winter.


01:21:46.974 --> 01:21:49.664
Can Maggie give
Sally a ride home?


01:22:18.433 --> 01:22:20.793
We used to make something here.


01:22:20.889 --> 01:22:23.277
Back before we got
lost in the paperwork.


01:22:23.373 --> 01:22:25.682
At one time we had
a frigate right here.


01:22:25.778 --> 01:22:27.910
Back there, a guided
missile cruiser.


01:22:28.006 --> 01:22:31.185
Phil started out
here in hull assembly.


01:22:32.628 --> 01:22:35.970
He was a skinny little
bastard, fearless.


01:22:36.121 --> 01:22:38.024
He'd hang upside down
all day long in...


01:22:38.120 --> 01:22:39.827
a bosuns chair,
seventy feet off the


01:22:39.923 --> 01:22:41.702
shop floor, welding
an inside seam.


01:22:41.798 --> 01:22:45.098
I mean... Jesus!


01:22:48.512 --> 01:22:50.939
Two thousand men a
shift, three shifts a day.


01:22:51.035 --> 01:22:55.192
Six thousand men earned an
honest wage in that room.


01:22:56.915 --> 01:22:59.279
Fed their kids, bought homes,


01:23:00.713 --> 01:23:03.572
Made enough to send
their kids to college,


01:23:03.667 --> 01:23:05.586
and buy a second car.


01:23:08.001 --> 01:23:10.669
Building something
they could see.


01:23:10.765 --> 01:23:13.594
Not just figures
on a balance sheet,


01:23:13.689 --> 01:23:17.939
but a ship. They could
see, smell, touch.


01:23:21.891 --> 01:23:26.049
Those men knew their worth,
they knew who they were.


01:23:30.312 --> 01:23:31.857
One day you're
making fifty dollars,


01:23:31.952 --> 01:23:36.297
the next day five thousand,
and then one day five million.


01:23:36.393 --> 01:23:40.163
You start out with a crazy
plan, take insane risks,


01:23:40.259 --> 01:23:42.618
barely make enough money
to feed your family.


01:23:42.714 --> 01:23:44.632
not a chance in hell
you're going to succeed.


01:23:44.728 --> 01:23:46.861
Then all of a sudden,
you've got all...


01:23:46.957 --> 01:23:49.648
these things and you're
terrified of losing them.


01:23:49.744 --> 01:23:51.902
Stock options, corporate jets,


01:23:51.998 --> 01:23:54.444
vacation homes in the Bahamas.


01:23:55.192 --> 01:24:00.073
You know? Truth is I liked
five hundred dollar lunches,


01:24:00.169 --> 01:24:03.267
and five thousand
dollar hotel suites.


01:24:07.815 --> 01:24:11.311
Now everything I spent
thirty years trying...


01:24:11.407 --> 01:24:14.994
to build for myself
and everybody else is...


01:24:16.101 --> 01:24:18.019
Gone.


01:24:50.056 --> 01:24:53.738
I'm sorry, Maggie.
- For what?


01:24:55.734 --> 01:24:57.652
For everything.


01:24:59.187 --> 01:25:03.061
For letting you down.
- You haven't let me down.


01:25:08.202 --> 01:25:10.926
Yeah, I did.


01:25:12.884 --> 01:25:15.085
You were never here before.


01:25:17.946 --> 01:25:19.865
And now you are.


01:25:33.907 --> 01:25:38.879
I think the dryer vent's clogged,
I'm going to go take a look.


01:25:39.509 --> 01:25:41.427
Hey, Bobby.
- Yeah.


01:25:44.420 --> 01:25:46.415
It can wait.


01:25:54.932 --> 01:25:56.850
Hello, Jim.


01:26:02.527 --> 01:26:05.262
Gene, how you been?


01:26:05.358 --> 01:26:09.270
Not good. I was recently
fired by my best friend.


01:26:12.350 --> 01:26:14.714
We missed you at the funeral.


01:26:15.305 --> 01:26:20.599
I was sorry to hear about
Phil. How's Lorna holding up?


01:26:24.396 --> 01:26:27.850
We built something
here, Jim. Together.


01:26:29.384 --> 01:26:32.770
Together; wasn't just you,
wasn't just me, it was all of us.


01:26:32.866 --> 01:26:35.393
They got a paycheck every week.


01:26:35.868 --> 01:26:38.678
Medical if they got sick,
disability if they got hurt.


01:26:38.774 --> 01:26:40.981
Hell, it's a business,
not a charity.


01:26:41.077 --> 01:26:42.518
Who took home twenty
two million last year,


01:26:42.613 --> 01:26:43.916
and these people
have lost their homes,


01:26:44.012 --> 01:26:46.467
their marriages, the
respect of their children.


01:26:46.563 --> 01:26:50.476
We did what the market
required of us to survive!


01:26:54.783 --> 01:26:57.133
The board accepted
Allied's bid last night.


01:26:57.229 --> 01:26:59.635
Thirty-nine billion at
ninety-seven a share.


01:26:59.731 --> 01:27:01.649
I'm sorry.
- Don't be.


01:27:02.033 --> 01:27:05.362
My shares are worth
six hundred million.


01:27:05.458 --> 01:27:07.376
Congratulations.


01:27:07.788 --> 01:27:09.989
What are yours worth, Gene?


01:27:14.771 --> 01:27:16.689
I have to get to work.


01:27:59.697 --> 01:28:01.615
Give me that ball.


01:28:01.693 --> 01:28:03.611
Give me the ball.


01:28:06.335 --> 01:28:10.981
Play your position, all right?
You're in trouble now, kid!


01:28:32.308 --> 01:28:33.872
Hey, Bobby.
- Yeah.


01:28:33.968 --> 01:28:38.125
Gene McClary is on the
phone, something about a job.


01:28:38.927 --> 01:28:43.410
Get some more eighteen inch
sinkers, I'll be right back.


01:28:50.417 --> 01:28:52.455
What are you waiting for?


01:29:24.217 --> 01:29:26.135
Working Sundays now?


01:29:27.900 --> 01:29:31.813
Deirdre says you've been
out here every weekend.


01:29:32.044 --> 01:29:33.933
You losing money
on this job, Jack?


01:29:34.029 --> 01:29:37.262
A bit.
- Because of me?


01:29:42.250 --> 01:29:44.715
Sometimes I'm up,
sometimes I'm down.


01:29:44.811 --> 01:29:47.093
It all comes out in the end.


01:29:49.577 --> 01:29:52.580
I got a call from a guy
today, I used to work for.


01:29:52.676 --> 01:29:55.697
He offered me a job.
- Yeah, decent pay?


01:29:55.793 --> 01:29:59.245
Eighty.
- Thousand?


01:30:01.893 --> 01:30:04.583
It's half of what
I used to make.


01:30:05.116 --> 01:30:07.561
The world's a fucked-up place.


01:30:09.911 --> 01:30:14.394
Actually I was thinking about
staying on with you, Jack.


01:30:16.088 --> 01:30:18.832
At my old job I was
scared all the time...


01:30:18.928 --> 01:30:22.295
Quarterly cost reports,
young guys coming up.


01:30:22.391 --> 01:30:25.958
Losing an account, or
who's getting ahead of me.


01:30:26.053 --> 01:30:28.615
Can I be honest with you, Bobby?
- Yeah.


01:30:28.711 --> 01:30:33.199
You should take that job,
you're a shitty carpenter.


01:30:37.995 --> 01:30:42.560
Christ, can't they make
these damn things any lighter?


01:30:49.888 --> 01:30:53.993
I can't pay you for today.


01:30:55.950 --> 01:30:59.129
Guess we better get
started, then. Huh?


01:30:59.518 --> 01:31:01.436
I... will... win. Why?


01:31:01.973 --> 01:31:03.891
Why?


01:31:04.046 --> 01:31:07.470
Because I have faith!
Courage! Enthusiasm!


01:31:07.959 --> 01:31:10.367
I... will... win.


01:31:10.463 --> 01:31:11.623
Why?


01:31:11.719 --> 01:31:15.833
Because I have faith!
Courage! Enthusiasm!


01:31:15.929 --> 01:31:17.847
I... will... win.


01:31:17.925 --> 01:31:19.248
Why?


01:31:19.343 --> 01:31:22.998
Because I have faith!
Courage! Enthusiasm!


01:31:25.875 --> 01:31:28.188
Can we get a pencil sharpener?
- Sure.


01:31:28.284 --> 01:31:29.790
The kind with the crank?


01:31:29.886 --> 01:31:32.493
Oh, the old fashioned
kind. I love those!


01:31:32.589 --> 01:31:35.439
McClary Maritime Associates.
- Well...


01:31:35.535 --> 01:31:37.280
Well, we don't have
any associates yet,


01:31:37.376 --> 01:31:38.892
but what the hell,
it sounds good.


01:31:38.987 --> 01:31:40.803
The printer's from
the dark ages, I'll...


01:31:40.899 --> 01:31:42.804
stop by Staples tomorrow
and get a new one.


01:31:42.900 --> 01:31:44.818
Okay.


01:31:45.614 --> 01:31:48.051
Nice office.
- It's not much.


01:31:49.279 --> 01:31:52.656
If I make the overhead the
first year, I'll be happy.


01:31:52.752 --> 01:31:55.021
I ran into Ben Wilson
the other day, he...


01:31:55.117 --> 01:31:57.882
said that you were going
out to possible investors.


01:31:57.978 --> 01:32:00.299
Yeah, I'm going to make
a move for Gloucester.


01:32:00.395 --> 01:32:02.313
The shipyards?
- Yeah.


01:32:02.994 --> 01:32:05.632
Allied doesn't want it,
nobody's got the skilled labor.


01:32:05.727 --> 01:32:07.589
I'll just renegotiate
with the unions,


01:32:07.685 --> 01:32:10.293
start slow, see if it'll grow...


01:32:12.068 --> 01:32:14.921
You think there's
a business there?


01:32:17.439 --> 01:32:19.722
Any time for lunch, Tuesday?


01:32:22.389 --> 01:32:24.307
No.


01:32:26.935 --> 01:32:32.402
I sat in rooms, and talked about
how to destroy people's lives.


01:32:33.035 --> 01:32:35.555
I thought I could do
more from the inside,


01:32:35.650 --> 01:32:37.620
save a few jobs
here and there...


01:32:37.716 --> 01:32:40.814
if I didn't do it,
somebody else would.


01:32:46.904 --> 01:32:50.281
Keep me in mind for
a possible associate.


01:32:51.048 --> 01:32:53.901
I think I may be
looking for a job.


01:33:23.966 --> 01:33:27.308
Say hello to Gene for me.
- How do I look?


01:33:27.802 --> 01:33:29.720
Highly employable.


01:33:35.859 --> 01:33:38.549
Go on, you don't
want to be late.


01:33:39.465 --> 01:33:41.576
Come here.
- I love you.


01:33:43.494 --> 01:33:45.412
I love you.


01:34:24.852 --> 01:34:27.206
All right, I hope you had
your fill of sitting around...


01:34:27.302 --> 01:34:29.313
the house all day watching
"The Price Is Right".


01:34:29.409 --> 01:34:30.656
It's time to get working, now.


01:34:30.752 --> 01:34:33.187
Don't complain about the
luxury accomodations here.


01:34:33.283 --> 01:34:35.873
Gene's basically kick starting
this thing on his AmEx card.


01:34:35.969 --> 01:34:37.637
You want to impress a client,


01:34:37.733 --> 01:34:40.352
take them to the Upper
Crust, buy them a slice.


01:34:40.448 --> 01:34:42.637
Diane, you need to do some
seller financing and...


01:34:42.733 --> 01:34:44.965
long term lease backs for
our in-state competitors.


01:34:45.061 --> 01:34:47.117
So run financials on our
old customers, vendors,


01:34:47.212 --> 01:34:49.004
capital expenditure
budgets, future needs.


01:34:49.100 --> 01:34:49.503
You got it.


01:34:49.599 --> 01:34:50.413
Okay.


01:34:50.509 --> 01:34:52.447
Conal, we need our
union guys back.


01:34:52.543 --> 01:34:54.193
How many?
- I don't know.


01:34:54.289 --> 01:34:55.821
A hundred? Something like
that, start with the local,


01:34:55.917 --> 01:34:56.495
see who is available.


01:34:56.591 --> 01:34:58.087
I'm betting everyone.


01:34:58.183 --> 01:35:02.307
Mechanics, machinists,
fabricators, welders, engineers,


01:35:02.403 --> 01:35:03.727
start with the crew chiefs.


01:35:03.823 --> 01:35:05.146
If we work as hard
in here every day,


01:35:05.241 --> 01:35:07.870
as we did trying to get a
job, we're going to be alright.


01:35:07.966 --> 01:35:09.616
What's the worst
thing they can do?


01:35:09.712 --> 01:35:11.630
Fire us?


01:35:18.712 --> 01:35:38.630
<b><font color=yellow>Resync
by GP Mobiles</font></b>

